    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "ACS:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " preferred over opioids for CP. Give SL first, then a cont IV drip if needed for pain, HTN or pulm edema. Don't give if SBP < 90 mm Hg or SBP has fallen > 30 mm Hg from baseline. Giving it to limit infarct size = ⍉longer recommended."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "IV NTG:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " start @ 5 mcg/min and increase by 2.5–5 mcg every few minutes until the needed response."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Also contraindicated w sGC stimulators such as riociguat (hypotension)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Contraindicated in severe anemia (methemoglobin can worsen it). May aggravate angina from HCM. Severe hypotension can occur even w sm doses, esp w aortic or MS, constrictive pericarditis, vol depletion or existing hypotension."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "OD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " severe hypotension, throbbing HA, methemoglobinemia w cyanosis, syncope. ⍉specific antagonist: raise central fluid vol (shock position, IV saline); methylene blue 1–2 mg/kg IV for methemoglobinemia unless G6PD deficiency; Epi = ineffective."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
